;; PgBouncer auth file. Copy to userlist.txt (git-ignored), fill in the secret and
;; place the same file on all three database hosts, then chmod 600.
;;
;; Format: "username" "secret"
;;
;; Simplest: the plaintext CRIMSON_APP_PASSWORD from postgres-ha/.env, the password
;; in the app's DATABASE_URL. With auth_type = scram-sha-256 PgBouncer uses it both
;; to verify the app and to log in to PostgreSQL. It already sits in .env on these
;; hosts, so the file adds no new exposure.
;;
;; More secure: the SCRAM verifier instead (it starts with SCRAM-SHA-256$). README
;; step 1 has the read-only query that prints the line.

"crimson" "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CRIMSON_APP_PASSWORD"
